{"availability":"available","full":"ixlab/vidformer","name":"vidformer","description":"A drop-in declarative optimization framework for rendering video data visualizations.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":69,"forks":6,"created":"2024-08-15T00:26:31Z","updated":"2026-10-05T13:24:05Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ixlab.github.io/vidformer/","topics":["declarative-video-editing","video","video-query","visualization"],"demo":"https://ixlab.github.io/vidformer/playground/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:06:45.896Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:06:45.896Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:06:45.896Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:21:14.789Z","stars":68,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-12T19:06:45.896Z","stars":69,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A research project for accelerating video/data visualization. See the preprint on arXiv for details.","Developed by the OSU Interactive Data Systems Lab.","Vidformer efficiently transforms videos, enabling faster annotation, editing, and processing of video data—without having to focus on performance. Just swap import cv2 with import vidformer.cv2 as cv2 to see video outputs instantly."],"features":["Transparent Optimization: Vidformer optimizes the execution of declarative specifications just like a relational database optimizes relational queries.","Lazy/Deferred Rendering: Video results can be retrieved on-demand, allowing for practically instantaneous playback of video results.","OpenCV: A cv2-compatible interface ensures both you (and LLMs) can use existing knowledge and code.","Supervision: Supervision-compatible annotators make visualizing computer vision models trivial.","FFmpeg: Built on the same libraries, codecs, and formats that run the world."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ixlab/vidformer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"62dd38cf53e62916348c1f883a5b62ef14e64c26bb5e206a9d7